%N A110133 Numbers which are the sides that belong to only one primitive Pythagorean triangle.
%C A110133 Powers of 2 starting with 2^2=4 and powers of primes of form 4k+3; none is a hypotenuse. - _Ray Chandler_, Jul 21 2005
%C A110133 Along with 2, the natural numbers that are Gaussian prime powers. - _Morgan L. Owens_, Nov 21 2014
%e A110133 From _Bernard Schott_, Oct 15 2026: (Start)
%e A110133 a(1) = 3 and a(2) = 4 because of (3,4,5);
%e A110133 a(3) = 7 because of (7,24,25) but 24 is not a term since (24,143,145) is another primitive Pythagorean triple.
%e A110133 a(4) = 8 because of (8,15,17) but 15 is not a term since (15,112,113) is another primitive Pythagorean triple. (End)
%Y A110133 Cf. A024357, A024363, A110134, A002145.
